
  <sn><md>### Comments in C

Comments are used to `provide information` to people reading the source code. They are `ignored by the compiler` and therefore do not affect the actual meaning or behavior of the program.

C supports two main comment syntaxes:

```c
/* Traditional comment */
```

and

```c
// Single-line comment
```

The `/* */` syntax is the original C comment style, while `//` was introduced later. Documentation systems may also use specially formatted comments to automatically generate documentation from source code.
</md></sn>
